DUMMY_PRD_TEXT = '{"executive_summary": "CobolCraft is a COBOL game server platform with two integrated subsystems: (1) a deterministic code generation pipeline and (2) a real-time multiplayer runtime server. Repository scale is **189 COBOL programs**, **67 copybooks**, **273 total files**. [CONFIRMED] [CODE-ONLY]\\n\\nThis PRD defines implementation-ready requirements with measurable acceptance criteria, explicit schemas, verification methods, and quantified non-functional targets. It is grounded in analyzed modules including `codegen/*`, `src/*` (blocks, commands, packets, inventory, players, entities, world, encoding, parsers), and `tests/*`. [CONFIRMED] [CODE-ONLY]\\n\\nCore confirmed capabilities include:\\n- Strict codegen invocation validation (`DATADIR`, `OUTDIR`, `TPLDIR`) and fixed generator order. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Registry ingestion from `reports/registries.json` using `protocol_id + 1` indexing and post-parse integrity assertions. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Packet-driven runtime with callback-dispatched behaviors for windows, blocks, items, entities, and commands. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Inventory/window mutation protection via state-id synchronization and safe packet-drain abort behavior. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Player lifecycle with file persistence (`<level>/playerdata/<uuid>.dat`), gzip-compressed NBT save path, and tolerant load semantics. [CONFIRMED]\\n- World/chunk mutation and PLAY-state client notifications with chunk dirty tracking. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\nKnown boundary of evidence: no product docs were provided; this PRD is **code-derived** and some copybook internals remain partially unexpanded in source extracts. [UNKNOWN] [CODE-ONLY]", "system_overview": "## Purpose and Scope\\nCobolCraft provides:\\n1. **Offline code generation**: produce COBOL source artifacts from JSON + templates.\\n2. **Online runtime server**: manage clients, players, world state, packets, commands, inventory/windows, entities, and persistence. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## In-Scope Subsystems\\n- **Codegen**: argument validation, shared path setup, registry loader, template load/eval/optimize, file emit (`Start/Append/End`), and generators (packets, registries, items, blocks loot table). [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Runtime**:\\n  - Packet decoding and dispatch (handshake/configuration/status/play serverbound handlers observed). [CONFIRMED]\\n  - Commands (`gamemode`, `help`, `kill`, `save`, `say`, `stop`, `time`, `whitelist`). [CONFIRMED]\\n  - Players (connect/load/tick/move/damage/disconnect/save). [CONFIRMED]\\n  - World/chunks/blocks/block entities (get/set/notify/save paths). [CONFIRMED]\\n  - Inventory + windows (player/crafting callbacks for sync/close/set-slot/drop). [CONFIRMED]\\n  - Entity callback framework and item-entity simulation. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- External database integrations (not observed). [UNKNOWN]\\n- Formal protocol compatibility guarantees beyond implemented handlers. [UNKNOWN]\\n\\n## Architectural Style\\n- Shared global runtime state via EXTERNAL copybooks. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Program-pointer callback polymorphism (`PROGRAM-POINTER`) for extensibility. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Fail-fast assertions in parse/codegen and many utility paths. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Predominantly single-process, stateful server loop behavior. [INFERRED]\\n\\n## Glossary\\n- **protocol_id**: integer identifier from registry JSON used as authoritative index; stored at `id+1`. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **VarInt**: variable-length integer encoding used in packet fields. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **state synchronization**: client/server window state-id match required before applying inventory mutation. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **chunk section**: vertical 16-block slice; observed section count constant 24 with Y range mapping. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **PLAY-state client**: connected client whose protocol state equals runtime play state constant. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## Assumptions and Constraints\\n- Runtime uses fixed-capacity arrays (e.g., player capacity 100, inventory slot structures fixed). [CONFIRMED]\\n- World Y bounds enforced at -64..319. [CONFIRMED]\\n- JSON/template buffers are statically large; memory profile is bounded but heavy. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Compiler/runtime dependencies include GnuCOBOL-sensitive paths (`GCVERSION` conditionals observed). [CONFIRMED]", "functional_requirements": "## FR-1 Codegen Invocation & Orchestration\\n**The system shall** require non-blank `DATADIR`, `OUTDIR`, and `TPLDIR` arguments before generation begins. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Input:** CLI chaining arguments to `CodegenMain`.\\n- **Processing:** Validate blanks/omissions; on valid input call `Codegen-SetDataDirectory`, `Codegen-SetOutputDirectory`, `Codegen-SetTemplateDirectory`, `CG-LoadRegistries`, then generators in fixed order: `CG-Packets`, `CG-Registries`, `CG-Items`, `CG-BlocksLootTable`.\\n- **Output:** Exit code and generated files.\\n- **Acceptance criteria:**\\n  1. Given any missing/blank argument, process exits with code `1`, emits usage text to STDERR, and creates **0** files in OUTDIR. [CONFIRMED]\\n  2. Given all arguments present, each of the 4 generators is invoked exactly once in specified order. [CONFIRMED]\\n  3. On successful run, generated output file handles are created, written, and closed (`Codegen-Start/Append/End`). [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## FR-2 Registry Ingestion\\n**The system shall** parse `reports/registries.json` and load in-memory registry tables keyed by `protocol_id+1`. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Input:** JSON document from `Codegen-ReadDataFile`.\\n- **Processing:** Parse root object; for each registry parse `protocol_id`; parse `entries`; require entry `protocol_id`; skip unknown JSON members; post-parse assert contiguous populated names over counted ranges.\\n- **Output:** Populated `DD-REGISTRIES` (`REGISTRY-COUNT`, registry names, entry counts/names).\\n- **Acceptance criteria:**\\n  1. Any JSON parse failure causes assertion termination with non-zero exit. [CONFIRMED]\\n  2. Missing entry `protocol_id` causes assertion failure (`CURRENT-ENTRY-ID >= 0` check). [CONFIRMED]\\n  3. Registry and entry names resolve at array index `protocol_id+1`. [CONFIRMED]\\n  4. Gap in counted ranges fails post-parse assertions (integrity check phase). [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## FR-3 Template-Driven Generation\\n**The system shall** support template variable replacement with transforms and callback dispatch. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Input:** Template file, callback pointer, output buffer.\\n- **Processing:** Load template, parse `$var[:transform=value]$`, evaluate via replacer callback, apply transforms (`indent=<n>`, `newline=after`), optional optimizer pass.\\n- **Output:** Generated source text appended to output files.\\n- **Acceptance criteria:**\\n  1. Unknown transform name/value causes assertion failure (`ASSERT-FAILED`). [CONFIRMED]\\n  2. Variable table supports up to 16 placeholders per template structure instance. [CONFIRMED]\\n  3. `indent` transform inserts spaces after newline boundaries in copied output. [CONFIRMED]\\n  4. `newline=after` enforces trailing newline handling per variable rule. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## FR-4 Command Processing\\n**The system shall** register command trees and execute command callbacks with argument validation and user feedback. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Input:** Serverbound chat command packet text (`RecvPacket-ChatCommand`) and parsed command parts.\\n- **Processing:** Validate arity/syntax; dispatch by command node; mutate runtime state; send chat/system packets.\\n- **Output:** Command effects and responses.\\n- **Acceptance criteria:**\\n  1. Invalid arity/syntax sets usage-print behavior (e.g., `LK-PRINT-USAGE=1`) without unintended state mutation. [CONFIRMED]\\n  2. `/whitelist on|off` persists `SP-WHITELIST-ENABLE` via `ServerProperties-Write`. [CONFIRMED]\\n  3. `/kill` resolves `minecraft:generic_kill` damage type and invokes `Players-Damage` with lethal amount. [CONFIRMED]\\n  4. `/time set day|noon|night|midnight|<n>` maps aliases to 1000/6000/13000/18000 or numeric `NUMVAL`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## FR-5 Inventory & Window Interaction\\n**The system shall** process container click packets with synchronization guards and callback-mediated mutation. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Input:** `window-id`, `state-id`, `slot`, `button`, `mode`, changed slots, carried item.\\n- **Processing:** Validate window ownership and state alignment; resolve `WindowSetSlot/WindowDrop/WindowSync` callbacks by window type; apply mutations; optionally resync; safe-drain payload on early abort.\\n- **Output:** Updated inventory/window state and outbound sync/drop packets.\\n- **Acceptance criteria:**\\n  1. State-id mismatch triggers window/inventory synchronization and avoids unsafe mutation. [CONFIRMED]\\n  2. Unknown/missing callback pointers force abort path with payload drainage and no corruption. [CONFIRMED]\\n  3. Outside-window drop path (`slot=-999`) routes to world drop handling. [CONFIRMED]\\n  4. Early-abort must consume declared changed-slot payload count fully before return. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## FR-6 Player Lifecycle & Persistence\\n**The system shall** support connect, load defaults/restore, runtime updates, disconnect-save, and per-player file persistence. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Input:** client id, UUID/name, movement/damage events, disconnect trigger.\\n- **Processing:** Allocate slot, initialize defaults, attempt load, update tick/move/damage, execute close callbacks on disconnect, save player data.\\n- **Output:** In-memory player state and persisted player file.\\n- **Acceptance criteria:**\\n  1. On connect with capacity available, returns non-zero player id and binds `PLAYER-CLIENT`. [CONFIRMED]\\n  2. On load failure, connection proceeds with initialized defaults (non-fatal). [CONFIRMED]\\n  3. Disconnect invokes window close callback (if available), then save, then clears client binding. [CONFIRMED]\\n  4. Save writes gzip-compressed NBT to `<level>/playerdata/<uuid>.dat`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## FR-7 World/Block/Block-Entity Mutation\\n**The system shall** safely mutate world blocks and block entities by chunk-indexed coordinates and notify PLAY clients. [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Input:** world position and target block/entity identifiers.\\n- **Processing:** Resolve chunk/section/block indices, mutate state, maintain counters/dirty flags, cleanup stale block entities when block type changes, broadcast updates.\\n- **Output:** Updated chunk state, dirty markers, outbound block/block-entity/world-event packets.\\n- **Acceptance criteria:**\\n  1. Missing chunk in setters performs no-op without crash. [CONFIRMED]\\n  2. Any block or notify mutation sets chunk dirty flag for persistence. [CONFIRMED]\\n  3. Block set to air can emit block-break world event with previous block context. [CONFIRMED]\\n  4. Block-entity set allocates data through registered allocate callback when available. [CONFIRMED]", "data_model": "## Entity Schemas (implementation-focused)\\n\\n### 1) Client [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Primary key:** `client_id` (array index, 1..MAX-CLIENTS) [INFERRED]\\n- **Core fields (observed):**\\n  - `CLIENT-STATE` (int enum) [CONFIRMED]\\n  - `CLIENT-PLAYER` (uint32 player id link; 0 = none) [CONFIRMED]\\n  - `TELEPORT-SENT`, `TELEPORT-RECV` (int32) [CONFIRMED]\\n  - `KEEPALIVE-SENT`, `KEEPALIVE-RECV` (int64) [CONFIRMED]\\n  - `CONFIG-FINISH` flag (uint8) [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Cardinality:** Client -> Player is **0..1** by `CLIENT-PLAYER`; Player -> Client is **0..1** by `PLAYER-CLIENT`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n### 2) Player [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Primary key:** `player_id` (1..`PLAYER-CAPACITY`, value 100) [CONFIRMED]\\n- **Core fields:**\\n  - `PLAYER-CLIENT` (uint32 FK to Client; 0 disconnected)\\n  - `PLAYER-UUID` (X(16) bytes)\\n  - `PLAYER-NAME` (X(16))\\n  - Position/rotation/velocity (`FLOAT-LONG` / `FLOAT-SHORT`)\\n  - `PLAYER-HEALTH` (float32), food/saturation/xp levels\\n  - `PLAYER-GAMEMODE` (int enum 0..3)\\n  - `PLAYER-INVENTORY-SLOT` occurs 46 (`DD-INVENTORY-SLOT`)\\n  - `PLAYER-WINDOW-SLOT` occurs 54 (`DD-INVENTORY-SLOT`)\\n- **Nullability:** COBOL defaults imply non-null fixed fields; semantic emptiness via sentinel values (e.g., count 0, id -1/0). [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n### 3) InventorySlot (`DD-INVENTORY-SLOT`) [CONFIRMED]\\n- `SLOT-COUNT` (uint8)\\n- `SLOT-ID` (int32)\\n- `SLOT-NBT-LENGTH` (uint32)\\n- `SLOT-NBT-DATA` (X(1024))\\n- **Compatibility rule:** stackable when id equal and NBT payload exactly equal. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n### 4) Registry (`DD-REGISTRIES`) [CONFIRMED]\\n- `REGISTRY-COUNT`\\n- `REGISTRY-NAME(index)`\\n- `REGISTRY-ENTRY-COUNT(registry)`\\n- `REGISTRY-ENTRY-NAME(registry, entry)`\\n- **Indexing:** `protocol_id + 1` for registry and entries. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n### 5) Chunk (`DD-CHUNK-REF`) [CONFIRMED]\\n- `CHUNK-X`, `CHUNK-Z`\\n- Dirty flags: `CHUNK-DIRTY-BLOCKS`, `CHUNK-DIRTY-ENTITIES`\\n- `CHUNK-SECTION` occurs 24\\n  - `CHUNK-SECTION-BLOCK` occurs 4096 (uint32)\\n  - `CHUNK-SECTION-BIOME` occurs 64 (uint32)\\n- `CHUNK-BLOCK-ENTITY` occurs 98304 (with `DD-BLOCK-ENTITY`)\\n- `CHUNK-ENTITY-LIST` pointer\\n\\n### 6) World (`DD-WORLD`) [CONFIRMED]\\n- Global chunk table and world metadata (fields partially unexpanded). [UNKNOWN]\\n- Bounds rule enforced by `World-CheckBounds`: Y in [-64, 319]. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n### 7) Callback Registries (`DD-CALLBACKS` + linkage copybooks) [CONFIRMED]\\n- Program-pointer arrays keyed by type ids for:\\n  - Blocks: destroy/face/interact/replaceable/item/loot\\n  - Block entities: allocate/serialize/deserialize\\n  - Entities: serialize/deserialize/tick\\n  - Windows: sync/close/set-slot/drop\\n  - Items: use\\n\\n## Relationship Summary\\n- Client (0..1) <-> Player (0..1) via reciprocal id references. [CONFIRMED]\\n- World (1) -> Chunks (0..N), Chunk -> Sections (24 fixed), Section -> Blocks (4096 fixed). [CONFIRMED]\\n- Registry (1) -> Entries (0..N). [CONFIRMED]\\n- Player (1) -> Inventory slots (46 fixed), Window slots (54 fixed). [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## Enforcement Mechanisms\\n- No database FK constraints; integrity is enforced by runtime checks, assertions, and array index discipline. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Sentinel semantics: 0/-1/NULL pointer denote absence depending on field. [CONFIRMED]", "process_flows": "## Flow 1: Codegen Run\\n1. Validate args in `CodegenMain`.\\n   - If any missing/blank -> usage + return 1.\\n2. Set EXTERNAL directories.\\n3. Load registries via `CG-LoadRegistries`.\\n   - If parse/assert failure -> terminate.\\n4. Execute generators in order: packets -> registries -> items -> blocks loot table.\\n5. Each generator: `TemplateLoad -> TemplateEval -> (optional Optimize) -> Start/Append/End`.\\n\\n## Flow 2: Registry Parse with Integrity Gate\\n1. Read `reports/registries.json` fully.\\n2. Parse root object entries as registries.\\n3. For each registry:\\n   - Extract `protocol_id`; store name at `id+1`.\\n   - Parse `entries` object only; skip other members.\\n4. For each entry:\\n   - Require `protocol_id`; store entry name at `entry_id+1`.\\n5. Post-parse assertions:\\n   - For `1..REGISTRY-COUNT`, names must be non-blank.\\n   - For each registry counted entry range, entry names non-blank.\\n\\n## Flow 3: Command Execution (`/whitelist` example)\\n1. Packet `RecvPacket-ChatCommand` decodes command text.\\n2. `HandleCommand` resolves command tree node/callback.\\n3. `Callback-Execute` branch:\\n   - `reload`: `Whitelist-Read`\\n   - `on/off`: set property + `ServerProperties-Write`\\n   - `list`: build response (dynamic buffer fallback)\\n   - `add/remove`: resolve UUID, call `Whitelist-Add/Remove`\\n4. On IO failure: run common failure handler and return.\\n5. Send resulting chat feedback.\\n\\n## Flow 4: Container Click Decision Flow\\n1. Decode packet fields and changed-slot count.\\n2. Validate current window id.\\n   - Mismatch -> `AbortEarly` (drain payload) -> return.\\n3. Resolve callbacks by window type.\\n   - Missing required callback -> set sync required; `AbortEarly`; resync path.\\n4. Compare state ids.\\n   - Mismatch -> set sync required; `AbortEarly`.\\n5. Apply click mode logic (set-slot/drop/etc) through callbacks.\\n6. If sync required -> invoke window sync + inventory sync as needed.\\n\\n## Flow 5: Player Disconnect Transaction Boundary\\n1. Receive disconnect trigger with player id.\\n2. Resolve `WindowClose` callback by active window type.\\n3. If callback exists, invoke to reconcile cursor/crafting items.\\n4. Attempt `Players-SavePlayer`.\\n   - On save failure: log failure; disconnect still proceeds.\\n5. Clear `PLAYER-CLIENT` and related bindings.\\n\\n## Flow 6: Block Mutation\\n1. Compute chunk coordinates and indexes.\\n2. Find chunk index.\\n   - If missing -> no-op return.\\n3. Read existing block; if unchanged -> return.\\n4. Write new block id; update non-air counters and dirty flag.\\n5. If block type changed and block entity exists -> free old entity data.\\n6. Broadcast `BlockUpdate` to PLAY clients.\\n7. If new block is air -> optional break event packet.\\n\\n## Flow 7: Player Damage\\n1. Lazy init registry ids for damage/sound constants.\\n2. Apply guards:\\n   - dead player\\n   - creative immunity exceptions\\n   - hurt-time invulnerability exceptions\\n3. Subtract health; send health packet.\\n4. If alive -> pick and send hurt/fall sound.\\n5. If dead -> send entity death event to PLAY clients and broadcast death message.", "business_rules": "## Business Rules Table\\n\\n- **BR-001**: All three codegen directories are mandatory; invalid usage exits with code 1.  \\n  **Type:** Validation  \\n  **Verification:** CLI integration test with 7 permutations of missing args; expect exit=1 and zero outputs.  \\n  **Trace:** `CodegenMain.main`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-002**: Registry and entry names are stored at `protocol_id + 1`.  \\n  **Type:** Data integrity  \\n  **Verification:** Fixture with known ids; assert indexed names in `DD-REGISTRIES`.  \\n  **Trace:** `CG-LoadRegistries.ParseRegistry`, `ParseRegistryEntry`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-003**: Post-parse contiguous-range integrity assertions must pass for counted registry/entry ranges (no blank gaps).  \\n  **Type:** Data integrity  \\n  **Verification:** Negative fixture introducing id gap; expect assertion failure.  \\n  **Trace:** `CG-LoadRegistries` post-parse asserts. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-004**: Generic block registration assigns destroy/face/replaceable/item callbacks and hardness=1.0 to all states.  \\n  **Type:** Default behavior  \\n  **Verification:** Unit test over sampled state ids checks callback pointers + hardness value.  \\n  **Trace:** `RegisterBlock-Generic.main`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-005**: Generic block destroy drops loot only in survival/adventure modes.  \\n  **Type:** Gameplay  \\n  **Verification:** Simulated destroy across gamemodes 0/1/2/3; observe drop invocations only for 0/2.  \\n  **Trace:** `RegisterBlock-Generic.Callback-Destroy`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-006**: Whitelist on/off toggles must persist to server properties file.  \\n  **Type:** Persistence  \\n  **Verification:** Command integration test validates `SP-WHITELIST-ENABLE` and successful `ServerProperties-Write`.  \\n  **Trace:** `RegisterCommand-Whitelist.Callback-Execute`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-007**: Whitelist add/remove resolves player name->UUID and distinguishes IO failure vs state failure.  \\n  **Type:** Error handling  \\n  **Verification:** Mock UUID resolver + whitelist backend for success/io-fail/state-fail branches.  \\n  **Trace:** `RegisterCommand-Whitelist.Callback-Execute`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-008**: Container click state mismatch must trigger synchronization rather than unsafe mutation.  \\n  **Type:** Consistency  \\n  **Verification:** Inject stale `state-id`; assert no mutation and sync callback invocation.  \\n  **Trace:** `RecvPacket-ContainerClick.main`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-009**: Early-abort container handling must drain remaining changed-slot payload bytes.  \\n  **Type:** Protocol safety  \\n  **Verification:** Fuzz malformed packets; assert parser offset reaches end of declared slot payload region.  \\n  **Trace:** `RecvPacket-ContainerClick.AbortEarly`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-010**: Creative players are immune to damage except `generic_kill` and `out_of_world`.  \\n  **Type:** Gameplay  \\n  **Verification:** Damage matrix test for creative mode and damage types.  \\n  **Trace:** `Players-Damage`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-011**: Hurt-time invulnerability suppresses repeated damage except `generic_kill`.  \\n  **Type:** Gameplay  \\n  **Verification:** Apply rapid consecutive hits; verify suppression behavior.  \\n  **Trace:** `Players-Damage`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-012**: Death handling emits entity event and broadcasts type-specific message.  \\n  **Type:** Gameplay/UX  \\n  **Verification:** Lethal damage test for fall/generic_kill/out_of_world; assert message variant and event packet.  \\n  **Trace:** `Players-Damage.BuildDeathMessage`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-013**: World bounds are Y=-64..319 inclusive.  \\n  **Type:** Boundary  \\n  **Verification:** `World-CheckBounds` unit tests on -65,-64,319,320.  \\n  **Trace:** `World-CheckBounds`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-014**: Block/world notify mutations set chunk dirty and broadcast to PLAY clients.  \\n  **Type:** Persistence + replication  \\n  **Verification:** Mutate block then assert dirty flag and outbound notifications to PLAY-state clients only.  \\n  **Trace:** `World-SetBlock`, `World-NotifyChanged`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-015**: Player save path is `<level>/playerdata/<uuid>.dat` and save data is gzip-compressed NBT.  \\n  **Type:** Persistence format  \\n  **Verification:** Save player then inspect path and gzip magic bytes `1F8B`.  \\n  **Trace:** `Players-PlayerFileName`, `Players-SavePlayer`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-016**: Player load accepts gzip and non-gzip NBT payloads; unknown tags are skipped.  \\n  **Type:** Compatibility  \\n  **Verification:** Load compressed and uncompressed fixtures plus unknown tags; assert successful parse.  \\n  **Trace:** `Players-LoadPlayer`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-017**: Disconnect proceeds even when save fails; failure is logged.  \\n  **Type:** Transaction boundary  \\n  **Verification:** Force save failure during disconnect; assert player is still disconnected and error logged.  \\n  **Trace:** `Players-Disconnect`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-018**: Inventory store uses two-pass strategy: merge into compatible stacks, then place in empty slots; remainder remains in source slot.  \\n  **Type:** Inventory semantics  \\n  **Verification:** Controlled inventory fixtures for full/partial/no-fit scenarios.  \\n  **Trace:** `Inventory-StoreItem`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-019**: Inventory compatibility requires same item id and exact NBT payload equality.  \\n  **Type:** Inventory semantics  \\n  **Verification:** Pairwise item comparison tests across id/NBT differences.  \\n  **Trace:** `Inventory-CompareItems`. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n- **BR-020**: Item entities despawn when age > 6000 ticks.  \\n  **Type:** Entity lifecycle  \\n  **Verification:** Simulate tick progression and assert remove flag at threshold+1.  \\n  **Trace:** `src/entities/item.cob Callback-Tick`. [CONFIRMED]", "external_interfaces": "## File Interfaces\\n\\n### 1) Registry Input\\n- **Path:** `<DATADIR>/reports/registries.json`  \\n- **Mode:** read-all  \\n- **Schema (observed minimum):**\\n  - root object\\n  - each registry key -> object containing `protocol_id` (int) and `entries` (object)\\n  - each entry object must contain `protocol_id` (int)\\n- **Versioning:** no explicit schema version field observed. [UNKNOWN]\\n\\n### 2) Generated Source Output\\n- **Path pattern:** `<OUTDIR>/*.cob` (generator-specific names)\\n- **Mode:** create/write/close via `Codegen-Start/Append/End`\\n- **Encoding:** text COBOL source (line content template-driven)\\n\\n### 3) Player Data\\n- **Path:** `<level>/playerdata/<uuid>.dat`\\n- **Mode:** read-all/write-all\\n- **Format:** NBT payload; save path is gzip-compressed; load path tolerates compressed or plain NBT.\\n\\n### 4) World Region/Entity Storage\\n- **Path pattern:** `<level>/region/r.<x>.<z>.mca`, `<level>/entities/r.<x>.<z>.mca`\\n- **Mode:** chunk persistence via region-file subsystem\\n- **Format:** NBT serialization for chunk/section/block/entity payloads (detailed full schema partially unexpanded). [UNKNOWN]\\n\\n## Programmatic Interfaces (selected)\\n- `CodegenMain -> CG-LoadRegistries(DATADIR)`\\n- `CodegenMain -> CG-Packets|CG-Registries|CG-Items|CG-BlocksLootTable(OUTDIR,TPLDIR)`\\n- `RecvPacket-ContainerClick -> GetCallback-WindowSetSlot(WINDOW-TYPE, PTR)`\\n- `RegisterCommand-Whitelist -> Whitelist-Add(UUID, NAME, IO-FAILURE, STATE-FAILURE)`\\n- `Players-Damage -> SendPacket-EntityEvent(CLIENT, PLAYER, ENTITY-EVENT-DEATH)`\\n\\n## Network Protocol Interface\\n- **Inbound decode primitives:** `Decode-VarInt`, `Decode-String`, `Decode-Byte`, `Decode-Short`, `Decode-Long`, `Decode-Position`, `Decode-InventorySlot`, etc.\\n- **Outbound packet senders:** command/chat/system messages, inventory sync, block updates, entity events/sounds, login/play transitions.\\n- **Behavior:** stateful online packet handling with per-client state gating (handshake/status/login/config/play).\\n\\n## Encoding Notes\\n- VarInt and length-prefixed string semantics are explicitly implemented/tested.\\n- Packed position uses 26/12/26 bit layout.\\n- Some component parsing paths remain TODO in slot decode/encode branches.", "non_functional_requirements": "## NFR-1 Performance\\n- Packet handler execution for non-IO operations (decode + state mutate) shall complete in **< 5 ms p95** and **< 20 ms p99** under 100 concurrent clients in PLAY state. [INFERRED]\\n- Container click processing (FR-5 path) shall complete in **< 10 ms p95** and **< 50 ms p99** excluding network latency. [INFERRED]\\n- Codegen full run (all 4 generators) shall complete in **< 120 s** for baseline repository-sized input on reference hardware. [INFERRED]\\n\\n## NFR-2 Scalability\\n- Runtime shall support at least **100 concurrent players** per process (aligned with observed `PLAYER-CAPACITY=100`). [CONFIRMED]\\n- Runtime shall support configured client slots up to `MAX-CLIENTS` from server properties/state tables without overflow assertions. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Chunk state table operations shall remain bounded by configured world chunk capacity (observed fixed array model). [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## NFR-3 Reliability\\n- Critical parse/assert failures shall terminate process with non-zero exit (fail-fast) in codegen and parser-critical paths. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Inventory mismatch scenarios shall recover via sync and avoid silent state corruption; error path test pass rate target **100%** across fuzzed stale-state suites. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Player disconnect shall proceed even if save fails; failure must be logged in **100%** of simulated save-fail tests. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## NFR-4 Data Integrity\\n- Registry contiguous-id integrity checks shall be enforced on every codegen run; gap fixture must fail in **100%** runs. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Inventory compare/store behavior shall preserve item count conservation (input = stored + remainder + dropped) with **0 mismatches** in test suite. [INFERRED]\\n\\n## NFR-5 Security & Input Safety\\n- Chat/command payload length beyond 256 bytes shall be rejected with disconnect in **100%** of overlength tests. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Invalid protocol state transitions (e.g., bad handshake next-state, unexpected finish-config) shall disconnect client in **100%** of tests. [CONFIRMED]\\n\\n## NFR-6 Observability\\n- Runtime shall emit human-readable status/error logs for command failures, save failures, parse failures, and key lifecycle transitions using DISPLAY output. [CONFIRMED]\\n- Structured metrics are not currently implemented; minimum requirement is per-failure log line presence in test harness capture. [INFERRED]\\n\\n## NFR-7 Testability\\n- All FRs and BRs in this PRD shall map to at least one executable test (unit/integration/system), with target coverage: **FR 100%**, **BR 100%** trace-linked tests. [INFERRED]\\n- Regression suite runtime budget: **<= 15 minutes** CI wall time on reference runner. [INFERRED]\\n\\n## NFR-8 Portability/Compatibility\\n- Build and runtime shall support GnuCOBOL paths with `GCVERSION` conditional branches tested for both `<32` and `>=32` code paths where applicable. [CONFIRMED]", "risks": "## Risk Register\\n\\n- **R-001 Global shared state coupling**  \\n  **Severity:** MEDIUM (high change impact, moderate likelihood)  \\n  **Evidence:** extensive EXTERNAL copybook state usage. [CONFIRMED]  \\n  **Mitigation:** add invariant checks around state mutation APIs; expand integration tests for side effects.\\n\\n- **R-002 Assertion-driven termination in runtime paths**  \\n  **Severity:** MEDIUM  \\n  **Evidence:** ASSERT/ASSERT-FAILED in multiple parse/runtime utilities. [CONFIRMED]  \\n  **Mitigation:** classify assertions into recoverable vs fatal; convert recoverable paths to structured error returns.\\n\\n- **R-003 Fixed-size buffers and occurs limits**  \\n  **Severity:** MEDIUM  \\n  **Evidence:** static buffers (e.g., JSON up to 10,000,000; slot NBT 1024; template var occurs 0..16). [CONFIRMED]  \\n  **Mitigation:** enforce bounds tests and fuzzing; document operational limits; add graceful reject paths.\\n\\n- **R-004 Partial module extraction uncertainty**  \\n  **Severity:** MEDIUM  \\n  **Evidence:** some copybook/module internals not fully expanded in provided analysis. [UNKNOWN] [CODE-ONLY]  \\n  **Mitigation:** run full-source extraction pass and regenerate trace matrix before release sign-off.\\n\\n- **R-005 TODO/unfinished branches (loot/components/complex parsing)**  \\n  **Severity:** HIGH  \\n  **Evidence:** explicit TODO markers in loot/component handling and parser areas. [CONFIRMED]  \\n  **Mitigation:** prioritize TODO backlog with failing tests converted to passing acceptance tests; gate release on closure of critical TODOs.\\n\\n- **R-006 Protocol desync under high-frequency inventory interactions**  \\n  **Severity:** MEDIUM  \\n  **Evidence:** explicit resync and abort-drain logic implies known desync risk domain. [INFERRED]  \\n  **Mitigation:** packet-sequence fuzz testing, state snapshot assertions, and telemetry counters for resync frequency.\\n\\n- **R-007 Persistence compatibility and corruption handling**  \\n  **Severity:** MEDIUM  \\n  **Evidence:** load supports compressed/uncompressed + unknown tags skip; malformed payload behavior not fully specified. [CONFIRMED]  \\n  **Mitigation:** add corruption-detection tests and fallback quarantine flow for bad player files.\\n\\n- **R-008 Capacity ceiling risk (player cap and fixed tables)**  \\n  **Severity:** MEDIUM  \\n  **Evidence:** observed `PLAYER-CAPACITY=100` and fixed-array architecture. [CONFIRMED]  \\n  **Mitigation:** explicit capacity monitoring, admission control messaging, and roadmap for dynamic structures.\\n\\n## Residual Risk Acceptance Criteria\\n- No HIGH risks remain without an automated regression test and an owner-approved mitigation plan before production release. [INFERRED]\\n- MEDIUM risks must have documented runbook actions and monitoring signals before GA. [INFERRED]"}'

